<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAfrica money mkt shortage holds below 10 bln rand.</title>
<headline>SAfrica money mkt shortage holds below 10 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's money market shortage held below the ten billion mark at 9.686 billion rand on Tuesday from 9.499 billion rand on Monday, the Reserve Bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Three-month NCD rates extended their downward trend, moving lower to between 17.35 and 17.65 percent from 17.35 and 17.75 percent on Tuesday while the 90-day BA rate was steady at between 16.65 and 16.95 percent.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
